---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/economics.css';

const title = 'This boom already has revenue and profit.';
const subhead = 'The open question is the price paid for those earnings, and when private companies raise cash.';

const cards = {
  cycle: {
    kicker: 'Cycle read',
    figure: 'Still 1998',
    label: 'Real revenue, profit for the strongest',
    note: 'Late-1990s internet stocks were priced partly on page views. Today the leaders report revenue and profit. Euphoria can still price a real market too high; the question is when repricing comes.',
  },
  froth: {
    kicker: 'Edge froth',
    figure: '50 to 100 times',
    label: 'Late private rounds, price to revenue',
    note: 'Unproven teams raising at 50 to 100 times revenue look like late dot-com checks. A proven operator can defend a high multiple, a high price for each dollar of revenue. A thin wrapper, a product built on someone else\'s model, cannot keep one forever.',
  },
  raise: {
    kicker: 'Cash timing',
    figure: 'Raise open',
    label: 'Cash timing for founders',
    note: 'Delaying a raise to wait for a higher price risks a closed window. A late-stage employee selling a slice is not the same signal as an early founder cashing out.',
  },
};

const legend = [
  'How to read this: Still 1998 is the cycle read. 50 to 100 times is the froth in late private rounds. Raise open is cash timing for founders.',
  'A true repeat of 1999 would mean prices based on traffic counts again and late-stage sellers finding no buyers.',
];
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} - Rycode`}
  description={subhead}
  variant="economics"
>
  <article class="econ-digest">
    <header class="econ-digest-head">
      <h1 class="econ-digest-title">{title}</h1>
      <p class="econ-digest-subhead">{subhead}</p>
    </header>

    <aside class="econ-digest-rail" data-digest-rail data-digest-fallback="froth" data-digest-stretch="froth" aria-label="Digest, economics read">
      <p class="econ-digest-kicker">Digest · Economics read</p>
      <div class="econ-digest-viewport">
        <div class="econ-digest-stack">
          {Object.entries(cards).map(([key, card]) => (
            <article class="econ-card" id={`card-${key}`} data-card={key}>
              <p class="econ-card-kicker">{card.kicker}</p>
              <p class="econ-card-figure">{card.figure}</p>
              <p class="econ-card-label">{card.label}</p>
              <p class="econ-card-note">{card.note}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="econ-digest-legend">
        {legend.map((line) => <p>{line}</p>)}
      </div>
    </aside>

    <p class="econ-digest-lede">The question people keep asking is whether this boom feels like 1998 or 1999. Anyone who lived through early 2000 carries scar tissue. That question is not the same as an answer. Overfitting the old pattern is its own risk.</p>

    <section class="econ-digest-section" id="what-1999-meant" data-digest-section="cycle">
      <h2>What 1999 meant, and what people are afraid of repeating</h2>
      <p>In the late 1990s, internet companies were often valued on metrics that were not dollars. A study of internet stocks in 1998 and 1999 found that page views and unique visitors helped explain their prices, while net income did not. The crash in early 2000 wiped out long tails of companies. Every new bull market, that scar tissue asks the same question: is this a bubble again?</p>
      <article class="econ-card econ-card--inline">
        <p class="econ-card-kicker">{cards.cycle.kicker}</p>
        <p class="econ-card-figure">{cards.cycle.figure}</p>
        <p class="econ-card-label">{cards.cycle.label}</p>
        <p class="econ-card-note">{cards.cycle.note}</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="econ-digest-section" id="cash-quality" data-digest-section="froth">
      <h2>This cycle has dollars where the last scare cycle had vanity metrics</h2>
      <p>The distinction that matters now is cash quality. Nvidia, which sells the chips inside AI data centers, reported $96.2 billion of revenue and $59.7 billion of net income for the quarter ended 26 Jul 2026. Anthropic's revenue run rate, a yearly pace projected from current sales, topped $65 billion by the end of July, according to Reuters. Products are in market. Customers pay. Euphoria can still price a real market too high. The clock is when that repricing comes, not whether the revenue is real.</p>
      <article class="econ-card econ-card--inline">
        <p class="econ-card-kicker">{cards.froth.kicker}</p>
        <p class="econ-card-figure">{cards.froth.figure}</p>
        <p class="econ-card-label">{cards.froth.label}</p>
        <p class="econ-card-note">{cards.froth.note}</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="econ-digest-section" id="cash-timing" data-digest-section="raise">
      <h2>Cash timing is the founder problem inside the euphoria</h2>
      <p>If the cycle still has years of heat left, the practical question is not whether to deny the boom. It is when to take money off the table and when to raise. Delaying a raise for a higher price risks a closed window.</p>
      <article class="econ-card econ-card--inline">
        <p class="econ-card-kicker">{cards.raise.kicker}</p>
        <p class="econ-card-figure">{cards.raise.figure}</p>
        <p class="econ-card-label">{cards.raise.label}</p>
        <p class="econ-card-note">{cards.raise.note}</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <div class="econ-digest-legend econ-digest-legend--inline">
      {legend.map((line) => <p>{line}</p>)}
    </div>

    <p class="econ-digest-closer">Still 1998 means price carefully, raise when the window is open if you need the cash, and do not confuse a real profit cycle with a permission slip for every private beta to clear at a hundred times sales.</p>

    <section class="econ-digest-section econ-digest-sources" id="sources">
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=206648">Trueman, Wong, and Zhang, The Eyeballs Have It: Searching for the Value in Internet Stocks, Journal of Accounting Research, 2000</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027">NVIDIA, financial results for the second quarter of fiscal 2027, 26 Aug 2026</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.reuters.com/technology/anthropic-revenue-run-rate-tops-65-billion-source-says-2026-08-17/">Reuters, Anthropic revenue run rate tops $65 billion, 17 Aug 2026</a></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

  </article>
</Layout>

<script is:inline src="/digest-rail.js" defer></script>
